			<div class="content" id="post-content-4849773">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> ???</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> So basically, it’s a brandless watch that has a digital clock, sets an alarm and has a timer. It has some anomalous properties in it’s functions. The clock, when reset, will turn back time to when the current user first found the watch/scp, meaning that if it is taken off and put back on again, the original encounter will be when the watch turns back time to. The alarm function, if at set time, will instantly give the current user a boost of energy and, if asleep, will instantly wake them up. The timer has two main anomalous functions. When stopped, if the timer has already been started, time will be stopped until the timer is started again. In this time, the user can move around freely and perform many actions. If the timer is restarted, time will go back to when the timer was about to start. If the user wears it for more than 2 weeks, the watch/scp will attach itself onto the user and the user would be unable to take it off, as it is now part of the body. Further testing has not been done.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative</strong>:The scp was originally located in a watch store and it was then given to the scp foundation after complaints from customers reporting that their friends and family were acting weirdly and returned it after symptoms showed. The watch then went onto the possession of many people, though they returned it soon after realising it’s anomalous capabilities. In one case though, a D-class got hold of it and tried to use the timer to escape once they realised what it did, and then they tried to stop time and escape [REDACTED], but they were too slow and the guards there quickly terminated them. After this, testing with the scp will only be tested with trusted D-class and trusted Researchers. One test of this was when Dr. [REDACTED] first tested it. The test consisted of testing it’s capabilities if it will regenerate lost limbs, wounds or scars. Dr. [REDACTED] volunteered for testing and endured great pain. From testing, it’s found out that when using the timer to reset or using the clock, the harm done to the user’s body will have a black line around the perimeter of the wound, scar or lost limbs, slightly differing between types of harm. This is an indicator if anyone has used the scp.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> I don't really know this is really the first time I’m doing something like this.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> This is my first time here/writing.</p>

