														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4849707">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlight :</strong> No (not yet)</p>
<p><strong>Page Type :</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre :</strong> Drama</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch :</strong> An SCP that allows a woman to get pregnant without having any sexual intercourse with a man. The activation of the SCP’s abnormal properties requires a sacrifice consisting of human blood, water and animal bones. The SCP “steals” another woman's pregnancy in order to make the user pregnant, and children born this way might be “special”.</p>
<p><strong>Narrative :</strong> (( I want to use the idea of fertility and pregnancy, and put it as the central abnormal effect of this SCP. This idea is inspired by an old African legend, in which a young infertile woman, Akua, was given a doll that would supposedly help her get pregnant ; which it did, or at least according to the legend. The doll was transmitted from woman to woman, and disappeared after some time. ))</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The Foundation received reports of a secret tribe located somewhere in Africa, in which men and women were showing incredible physical and mental abilities (strength, logical thinking and great charisma). Its inhabitants didn’t show any sign of hostility towards the SCP Agents that were sent to the place.</p>
<p>Upon investigating, the Foundation discovered that the tribe worshipped a wooden doll. Thanks to the efforts of The Foundation’s Translators, the agents were able to engage in a discussion with the aborigens, and discovered the abnormal effects of the doll.<br />
The resulting births and “procreation” within the tribe were hence caused by the impact of the SCP’s abnormal effects : all of the inhabitants claimed to have a woman as their parent, and the idea of a father seemed strange to them.<br />
It was peculiar that the tribe was so sophisticated and well-developed, despite being isolated from the rest of the world (complex language, irrigation systems…).The way it managed to remain hidden, as well as its history remains unknown.</p>
<p>The wooden doll was recovered [stolen] by the Foundation in order to study its anomalous properties. This led to a battle, resulting in a total termination of the tribe’s members.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber :</strong> I find this SCP interesting because it deals with the subject of fertility in a curious way.</p>
<p>Additional Notes : N/A</p>

